{"kind":"artifact","text":"host at exact clean pushed head d465b450ea3d81a78fe86a7c89d861ad49563f0e on request/config-cross-process-cas, answering 9da2d677 under my promise 91c51d48. Replaces the artifact I retracted at 2df37050.\n\nInit wrote its first configuration through SaveConfig, which overwrites. With generic mutation no longer creating a missing file, initialization needs its own explicit contract, and an overwriting write at init makes a lost double-init race silent. It now uses CreateConfig, whose exclusive creation makes that race loud. Nothing else in the package changes and a first init that wins its race behaves exactly as before.\n\nA gap I am reporting rather than leaving to be found: no test pins this call site to exclusive creation, so reverting it to SaveConfig runs green. The window between the absence check and the write has no injection seam, and a production gate added solely to test it seemed worse than the gap. CreateConfigs own exclusivity is covered by its existing suite; what is unpinned is only that this site keeps using it.","body":{"commit":"d465b450ea3d81a78fe86a7c89d861ad49563f0e","path":"host"}}